  "conclusion": "Same-mode grouping is not an information bottleneck: every column remains channel 0 of some group, and v2 in_linear is a well-conditioned injective 3\u2192d map. A predictor that is perfect on ungrouped 1D/2D features can read the same coordinates out of grouped tokens. Frozen-v2 vs frozen-v1 checks on needles, buried-scale distractors, and XOR do not yield a grouped-only failure. A true adversary would need a rank-deficient in_linear, a collapse of the number of tokens (the unused 'valid' mode), or a training-time failure to invert the mixing \u2014 none of which hold for TabICLv2 inference."
